# Testing standards

## Requirements

- **New feature:** at least unit tests for non-trivial logic; integration test for API endpoints that mutate family data.
- **Bug fix:** add a regression test when reproduction is reasonable without flaky E2E.
- **Skip tests** only with a comment explaining why (e.g. blocked on harness) — not for convenience.

## Placement

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| API unit | `apps/api/tests/unit/test_<module>.py` |
| API integration | `apps/api/tests/integration/test_<flow>.py` |
| Mobile unit | Colocated `*.test.ts(x)` or `apps/mobile/__tests__/` |

## Practices

- Tests are deterministic: fixed clocks for due dates, recurrence, maintenance intervals.
- Use factories/fixtures per module; do not copy large JSON blobs across files.
- Integration tests must isolate tenants — two families, assert no cross-leak.
- Mock external OAuth/calendar APIs; never hit Google/Microsoft in CI.

## Completion gate

Agents must run the narrowest relevant suite (module tests) at minimum; full API + mobile test commands before claiming done when both stacks change.
